\section{Reading}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{Geometry comes back as WKB by default.}
\code{dbConnect(geometry = )} chooses: \code{"blob"}, the default,
returns raw vectors; \code{"wk"} returns \code{wk_wkb}, which \code{\link[sf:st_as_sfc]{sf::st_as_sfc()}} converts onward.
\href{https://duckdb.org/docs/current/sql/data_types/geometry}{\code{GEOMETRY}} is a core DuckDB type since 1.5,
so reading one needs no extension,
but the geometry functions are still \code{spatial}'s, and so is the CRS provider that resolves a name like \code{EPSG:4326}.
\item \strong{The column's CRS reaches R either way.}
It is an attribute on \code{wk_wkb}, and PROJJSON in the metadata of the \code{geoarrow.wkb} field an Arrow result carries,
and \code{\link[sf:st_crs]{sf::st_crs()}} reads the same CRS from both.
\item \strong{sf reads a result through GeoArrow in one call.}
\code{sf::st_as_sf(dbGetQueryArrow(con, sql))} gives an \code{sf} whose geometries and CRS equal the source's,
and \code{sf::st_as_sfc()} does the same for the \code{geoarrow_vctr} column of \code{as.data.frame()}.
Both methods are the geoarrow package's, so it has to be loaded first:
without it, \code{st_as_sf()} has no method for the stream.
A \code{NULL} geometry reads as an empty one.
\item \strong{The routes behind \code{dbSendQuery(arrow = TRUE)} fail on a CRS.}
\code{\link[=duckdb_fetch_arrow]{duckdb_fetch_arrow()}}, \code{\link[=duckdb_fetch_record_batch]{duckdb_fetch_record_batch()}} and \code{\link[arrow:to_arrow]{arrow::to_arrow()}}, which reads through them,
fail with \verb{INTERNAL Error: TransactionContext::ActiveTransaction called without active transaction} for a column with a CRS.
\code{\link[DBI:dbGetQueryArrow]{dbGetQueryArrow()}} reads it,
and so do those routes once the query casts the column to the bare type, as \code{geom::GEOMETRY}, which drops the CRS.
}
