\section{Writing}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{Text writes GEOMETRY through \code{field.types}.}
A \code{character} column of \code{\link[sf:st_as_text]{sf::st_as_text()}} output with \code{field.types = c(geom = "GEOMETRY")} lands a \code{GEOMETRY} column in one statement,
because the \code{VARCHAR} cast parses WKT;
spell the CRS into the type, as \code{"GEOMETRY('EPSG:4267')"}, to keep it, which needs \code{spatial} loaded.
WKB has no such cast:
\code{BLOB} to \code{GEOMETRY} is unimplemented, so the same call over \code{\link[sf:st_as_binary]{sf::st_as_binary()}} output fails,
and so do \code{\link[DBI:dbAppendTable]{dbAppendTable()}} and a parameter bound to a \code{GEOMETRY} cast.
\code{ST_GeomFromWKB()} does the conversion instead: per query, bound to \verb{?},
or once through \verb{ALTER TABLE … ALTER COLUMN … SET DATA TYPE GEOMETRY USING}, which drops the CRS because it names the bare type.
\item \strong{GeoArrow WKB writes GEOMETRY with its CRS.}
Encode the geometry column as WKB,
as \code{geoarrow::as_geoarrow_vctr(sf::st_geometry(x), schema = geoarrow::geoarrow_wkb(crs = sf::st_crs(x)))}
or as a \code{\link[wk:as_wkb]{wk::as_wkb()}} column,
and register \code{arrow::as_arrow_table(nanoarrow::as_nanoarrow_array_stream(df))} with \code{\link[=duckdb_register_arrow]{duckdb_register_arrow()}};
\verb{CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT} from the view writes a \code{GEOMETRY} column with the CRS,
which reads back into an \code{sf} equal to the one written.
With \code{spatial} loaded, the type names the CRS by its identifier, as \code{GEOMETRY('EPSG:4267')};
without it, it keeps the PROJJSON it came as, and \code{sf::st_crs()} reads the same CRS from both.
\item \strong{The other GeoArrow encodings do not land as GEOMETRY.}
What nanoarrow infers for an \code{sf} column, and what \code{\link[arrow:as_arrow_table]{arrow::as_arrow_table()}} makes of one, is a native encoding,
which lands as nested structs, as \verb{STRUCT(x DOUBLE, y DOUBLE)[][][]} for a multipolygon.
A native point converts in the query as \verb{geometry::POINT_2D::GEOMETRY};
a native polygon casts neither through \code{POLYGON_2D} nor directly.
\code{geoarrow_wkt()} lands as \code{VARCHAR}, which \verb{::GEOMETRY} parses, and \code{ST_SetCRS()} gives the CRS back.
geoarrow cannot write an \code{sfc} in the large or view layouts of WKB,
and DuckDB lands those layouts, as its own export makes them, as \code{GEOMETRY}.
\item \strong{An \code{sf} or \code{sfc} column is not written, and may not say so.}
A whole \code{sf} object handed to \code{\link[DBI:dbWriteTable]{dbWriteTable()}} fails inside sf's own \code{\link[DBI:dbDataType]{dbDataType()}} method,
