\section{The \code{spatial} extension's types}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{The \code{spatial} extension's own types are aliases, and read as what they alias.}
\code{POINT_2D}, \code{POINT_3D}, \code{POINT_4D}, \code{BOX_2D} and \code{BOX_2DF} are structs, and read as data frame columns;
\code{LINESTRING_2D} and \code{LINESTRING_3D} are lists of point structs, and read as lists of data frames;
\code{POLYGON_2D} and \code{POLYGON_3D} are lists of those rings, and read as lists of lists;
\code{WKB_BLOB} is a \code{BLOB}, and reads as raw vectors.
The same shapes write the plain struct or list, and \code{field.types} naming the alias casts back to it.
WKT does not parse into them, but they cast to and from \code{GEOMETRY} in the query, as \verb{'POINT (1 2)'::GEOMETRY::POINT_2D}.
Arrow carries the storage without the alias.
}
}

\section{Limitations and reference}{
\itemize{
\item An \code{sf} object or \code{sfc} column is not written; a \code{POINT} column writes silently as \code{DOUBLE[]}.
\item A \code{geoarrow_vctr} column writes its integer indices through \code{dbWriteTable()} and \code{dbWriteTableArrow()}.
\item WKB in a \code{BLOB} column, or a \code{wk_wkb} column outside Arrow, has no cast to \code{GEOMETRY}.
\item Of the GeoArrow encodings, only WKB lands as \code{GEOMETRY}.
\item Naming a CRS in a type needs \code{spatial} loaded, and \verb{ALTER ... SET DATA TYPE GEOMETRY} drops the CRS.
\item The routes behind \code{dbSendQuery(arrow = TRUE)}, \code{arrow::to_arrow()} among them, fail on a column with a CRS.
\item \code{\link[sf:st_read]{sf::st_read()}} of a table does not recognize a \code{GEOMETRY} column, and returns a data frame.
}

The geometry functions are the \href{https://duckdb.org/docs/current/core_extensions/spatial/overview}{\code{spatial} extension's} to document,
and every other type is documented in \link{duckdb_types}.
The surface is measured route by route in \href{https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-r/blob/main/experiments/2026-08-09-spatial-interop/README.md}{\verb{experiments/2026-08-09-spatial-interop/}},
through GeoArrow in \href{https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-r/blob/main/experiments/2026-09-27-geoarrow/README.md}{\verb{experiments/2026-09-27-geoarrow/}},
